    "extraction_notes": [
      "PDF SHA-256 verified as 8104064ebdacf6293f29ee3e64485abe4c198a51424e770e9ec1c4175bb40de5.",
      "The datasheet identifies the device as an NPN transistor and gives Rev:1.0; all three pages were examined.",
      "The hFE table gives a guaranteed range of 90 to 600 at IC=1.0 mA and VCE=6.0 V. The separate rank table gives L4=90-180, L5=135-270, L6=200-400, and L7=300-600; these rank ranges are not represented as typical values.",
      "VCE(sat) and VBE(sat) are guaranteed maximums at IC=100 mA and IB=10 mA; they are retained as typed maximum bounds.",
      "No tabulated Cobo or Cibo value is provided. Fig.6 contains usable Cib and Cob curves, but the figure does not state measurement frequency or terminal bias, so cibo and cobo remain null and the curves are reported separately.",
      "Fig.6 is captioned Power Derating Curve in the source, although its plotted axes and traces are capacitance versus reverse voltage; the source caption is preserved in the page citation.",
      "Fig.1 prints the collector-current axis unit as A while the plotted magnitude and microampere base-current labels indicate milliampere-scale curve levels; the axis label and plotted numeric levels are preserved without reinterpretation.",
      "Curve points are manual digitizations from the supplied plots and are approximate readings of the visible traces, not interpolated or invented points."
    ],
